course: dictionary
lesson: 3891
title: Freshen: one word, four meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the author means. Freshen is a verb, so it is something you do. Look at the words around it first.
explain: «Freshen up before dinner» means wash quickly and tidy yourself. «Freshen the room» means make it cleaner or newer, like opening the windows and letting in fresh air. Ask yourself what is being freshened: a person, a room, or the wind?
explain: «The winds will freshen this afternoon» in a weather report means the wind will get stronger and cooler. The weather is the clue. Try your meaning in the sentence: the winds will get stronger and cooler still makes sense, so you have it.
fact: Freshen is a verb: freshen, freshens, freshened, freshening.
fact: To freshen something means to make it cleaner, cooler or newer, as in «freshen the air».
fact: To freshen up means to wash quickly and tidy yourself, as in «freshen up before dinner».
fact: When the wind freshens, it gets stronger and cooler.
fact: To freshen a drink means to add more to it. An «air freshener» is something that makes a room smell fresh.
exercise: «Freshen up before dinner.» What does freshen up mean here? | Go for a long walk | Cook the dinner | *Wash quickly and tidy yourself | Eat dinner very fast
exercise: «The winds will freshen this afternoon.» What does freshen mean in this weather report? | Stop blowing completely | *Get stronger and cooler | Turn warm and still | Become very quiet
exercise: Mum says, «Let's freshen the room.» What is she going to do? | Move all the furniture out | Lock the door | *Make the room cleaner and fresher | Paint the room black
test: «We need to freshen the air in here.» What does freshen mean? | Fill the room with smoke | *Make the air cleaner and fresher | Make the air heavier and thicker | Stop the air from moving
test: Ruby says «freshen» only means to cook. Why is she wrong? | Freshen really does mean to cook | Freshen means to fall asleep | Freshen means to feel sick | *Freshen can mean to make something cleaner, cooler or newer
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The wind freshened, so we put on our jackets»? | Became very dark | Got warmer and slower | *Got stronger and cooler | Stopped blowing completely
